  "readingFromCode": "In the RC7 driver, pgStartAttempted becomes true only after initdb, the configuration files and the three configuration dry checks succeed, and postmaster.pid.saved is written only after pg_ctl start succeeds and postmaster.pid is read. The sysv check reports SYSV_IDENTITY_UNKNOWN when that saved file is absent and the start attempt cannot be ruled out. So initdb and the dry checks most likely passed, and the job most likely failed at pg_ctl start or the postmaster.pid read. This is an inference from code and the outer proof, not observed host output.",
